<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoveyzeh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Howeyzeh, Hawizeh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoveyzeh is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, near the marshes on the Iraqi border. From the 15th century it was the capital of the Musha'sha, a dynasty of Arab sayyids who ruled much of Khuzestan under Safavid overlordship. Its importance declined from the 18th century as the Karkheh changed course and power passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kab">Banu Ka'b</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoveyzeh.jpg" alt="Hoveyzeh" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milad Hamadi · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crisis_in_Hoveyzeh_County2022-02-08_38.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
